Description: CVE-2018-15607 already fixed in ImageMagick 7.1.1.43 (PNM size guard)
 Documentation-only placeholder. Debian trixie tracker still says vulnerable.
 The published PoC is rejected by coders/pnm.c from upstream 7.0.8-12.
Author: Root.io
Last-Update: 2026-10-06

--- /dev/null
+++ b/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE
+
+## CVE-2018-15607 — already present in Debian trixie imagemagick 7.1.1.43
+
+The [Debian security tracker](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2018-15607)
+lists `8:7.1.1.43+dfsg1-1+deb13u12` as **vulnerable** / `(unfixed)` / unimportant.
+No fixed version is recorded. Default `policy.xml` limits are noted as mitigation.
+
+The published issue is [ImageMagick #1255](https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/issues/1255):
+an 18-byte file `50 36 36 36 36 4c 36 38 36 36 36 36 36 36 1f 35 50 00` (`P6666L...`).
+That is a P6 PPM, parsed as width 66 and height 68666666, which used to force a
+multi-gigabyte pixel-cache allocation.
+
+Upstream commit [d843df088db5](https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/d843df088db5)
+(ImageMagick 7.0.8-12, issue #1295) added this guard to `coders/pnm.c` before
+`SetImageExtent`:
+
+    if ((MagickSizeType) (image->columns*image->rows/8) > GetBlobSize(image))
+      ThrowPNMException(CorruptImageError,"InsufficientImageDataInFile");
+
+That line is present in Debian trixie `coders/pnm.c`. For the published file the
+check is about 566499994 > 18, so the reader rejects the input. The same commit's
+SGI check (`columns*rows/255 > GetBlobSize`) is already in `coders/sgi.c`. The
+related VIFF check is
+[23acdce36514](https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/23acdce3651447328c6ef71ede20ee60637ba39d).
+
+### Verdict
+
+No further code patch. This file is a scanner/audit marker only.
+
+### References
+
+- https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2018-15607
+- https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/issues/1255
+- https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/d843df088db5
+- https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/23acdce3651447328c6ef71ede20ee60637ba39d
Description: CVE-2026-66011 - Fix memory leak in magick CLI on invalid options
 InterpretImageProperties() in MagickCore/property.c leaked the interpreted
 text buffer, the cloned property image and property ImageInfo on several
 early-error/allocation-failure paths (empty "%[]" escape, unbalanced braces,
 ResizeQuantumMemory/AcquireString failures). The MagickWand CLI command
 handler CLINoImageOperator() in MagickWand/operation.c leaked previously
 interpreted arg1/arg2 strings when re-interpreting them for the "set" and
 "clone" operators. In addition, the ImageInfo cloned inside the DrawInfo by
 AcquireMagickCLI()/CloneDrawInfo() was never released, leaking on every
 magick CLI invocation, including when invalid options abort processing.
 .
 This backport consolidates the InterpretImageProperties cleanup onto a single
 "cleanup:" goto label driving a status flag, frees the stale interpreted
 argument strings before re-interpreting them in the CLI operator, and frees
 the DrawInfo-embedded ImageInfo both at acquisition (wandcli.c) and at CLI
 teardown (magick-cli.c). Purely cosmetic upstream churn (comment removal,
 whitespace, variable-declaration restyling) is intentionally omitted to keep
 the backport minimal; the fx/hex/pixel local "status" variables are renamed
 to "fx_status" only to avoid shadowing the newly introduced function-level
 status flag.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/e3e69118c29064e2716ca89aab635ea95a15dd49
